# =============================================================================
# PASTE SOURCE — this file becomes `.gitignore` in the NEW repo, in Task 0.
#
# It is deliberately NOT a live dotfile here: `hackathon-bob/` is not the repo
# and never will be (Task 0 does `mkdir {name-slug}`), so a stray `.gitignore`
# in this folder would do nothing except confuse you at H+0.
#
#   Task 0, Step 4/4b:  cp ../docs/ready/gitignore.txt .gitignore
#
# Composed 2026-09-25 from SCHEDULE.md §4.2, which records the IBM template's
# contents verbatim (fetched and read 2026-09-24). This is the MERGED result:
# our own rules first, the template's appended under its own banner, negations
# last. Do not reorder — see "ORDER IS LOAD-BEARING" at the bottom.
# =============================================================================

# --- Ours (plan Task 0, Step 4) ----------------------------------------------
node_modules/
dist/
.vercel/
.DS_Store
*.local
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# THE LEADING SLASH IS LOAD-BEARING. Bob writes exports to the WORKSPACE ROOT.
# A gitignore pattern with no internal slash matches at EVERY directory level,
# so the unanchored form would also ignore bob_sessions/bob-task-*.json — the
# eligibility deliverable — and `git add` would report nothing and exit 0.
# Anchoring to the root forces each export to be MOVED into bob_sessions/
# deliberately (that is the ritual), while keeping the moved copies trackable.
/bob-task-*.json
/bob-task-*.md
/bob-task-*.png

# THE SCREENSHOT IS IGNORED EVEN AFTER IT IS FILED. This is deliberate and it is
# the one rule here that blocks a deliverable on purpose.
# tools/redact.mjs scrubs TEXT. It cannot read PIXELS. A task-summary screenshot
# can carry an account name, an email, a C:\Users\<you> path, a private branch
# name, other tasks in the side panel or a desktop notification — and a commit to
# a public repo is IRREVERSIBLE: a force-push clears neither forks nor IBM's
# scanner. So ritual.mjs files the .png into bob_sessions/ and does NOT stage it;
# it prints the exact `git add -f` line to paste once you have actually looked.
# This pattern is what makes "did not review it" the default outcome instead of
# "committed it blind".
#
# HOW TO ADD ONE (after eyeballing it):
#   git add -f bob_sessions/<team>_task<NN>_<slug>_summary.png
#
# BACKSTOP if you forget: Task 14 Step 1 counts screenshots with `git ls-files`,
# so an unreviewed shot surfaces as a count mismatch at H+29 while you are awake,
# not as a leak after submission. Do NOT "fix" that mismatch by deleting this
# rule — add the reviewed files with -f.
bob_sessions/*_summary.png

# --- IBM hackathon template safeguards (appended, not replacing the above) ---
# WATSONX HACKATHON - SECURITY .GITIGNORE
# NOTE: bob_sessions/ folder is REQUIRED for project submission. Live session
# files are excluded, but exported reports must be included.
.copilot/
.cursor/
.codeium/

