# Add project-specific patterns below

# --- Receipts negations: the template's GENERIC substring patterns over-match -
# ORDER IS LOAD-BEARING: a git negation only works if it comes AFTER the pattern
# it re-includes. These MUST stay below the template block above.

# COLLISION 1 — `*secret*` would silently un-track a file we already ship.
# It is a generic substring pattern, so it matches at every directory level.
!tools/secret-scan.test.mjs

# COLLISION 2 — `*token*` is a live hazard for THIS project specifically:
# Receipts is *about* token counts. Any file later named tokens.css /
# context-tokens.md / token-budget.json vanishes from `git add` with exit 0 and
# no warning. Our design tokens live in src/index.css today and are safe.
# IF YOU EVER NAME A FILE WITH "token" IN IT, ADD ITS NEGATION IN THE SAME COMMIT.

# Verify before the first push — all five must behave as commented:
#   git check-ignore -v tools/secret-scan.test.mjs   # prints NOTHING (exit 1)
#   git check-ignore -v .env                         # prints a match (exit 0)
#   git check-ignore -v src/index.css                # prints NOTHING (exit 1)
#   git check-ignore -v bob_sessions/x_summary.png   # prints a match (exit 0)
#   git check-ignore -v bob_sessions/x_export.json   # prints NOTHING (exit 1)
#
# The last two are a PAIR and both matter. If the .json line ever starts printing
# a match, the screenshot rule has been widened and the app's own input format is
# now being silently dropped from `git add` with exit 0 and no warning.

.vercel
.env*

# internal submission working copy (video script, form paste copy) - not product
docs/submission/
